<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands</h1><p class="st-meta">1947 CE – 1994 CE · capital Honolulu; later Guam, Saipan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A United Nations strategic trust territory in Micronesia administered by the United States, scene of nuclear tests, which split into four modern states.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>American forces captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/south-seas-mandate">South Seas Mandate</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. In 1947 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> placed the Marshall, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-islands">Caroline</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-mariana-islands">Northern Mariana Islands</a> under American administration as the only strategic trust territory, giving the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> the right to fortify them.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-navy">US Navy</a> governed until 1951, then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> of the Interior, with headquarters moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saipan">Saipan</a> in 1962. From 1946 to 1958 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> conducted 67 nuclear tests at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bikini-atoll">Bikini</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enewetak">Enewetak</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castle-bravo">Castle Bravo</a> explosion of 1954, which contaminated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rongelap">Rongelap</a>. Development was neglected until the 1960s. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-micronesia">Congress of Micronesia</a>, created in 1965, became the forum for negotiating the islands' future.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The districts chose separate paths: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-mariana-islands">Northern Mariana Islands</a> became a US commonwealth, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federated-states-of-micronesia">Federated States of Micronesia</a> gained independence in free association in 1986. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palau">Palau's</a> compact took effect in 1994, ending the trusteeship.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/trust-territory-of-the-pacific-islands.jpg" alt="Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands" width="320" height="169"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Trust_Territory_of_the_Pacific_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1947 CE – 1994 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Honolulu; later Guam, Saipan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism, Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Marshallese, Chuukese, Palauan, Chamorro</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/palau">Palau</a>, <a href="/countries/micronesia">Micronesia</a>, Northern Mariana Islands, <a href="/countries/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>TTPI</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1970&amp;focus=trust-territory-of-the-pacific-islands" aria-label="Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8868 1786 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9188 2042L8721 2159M9188 2042L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8721 2159h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9188 2042h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9188 2042h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1970&amp;focus=trust-territory-of-the-pacific-islands">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
